    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9b1df1198e544edea0f3c16f7e6f7488",
      "statement": "A node that cannot reach the bucket cannot renew or replicate, so when its published expiry passes it fences itself, stops each active cell, fails requests, and exits with code 3 after logging a `SELF-FENCE:` line; the fence writes nothing to the bucket and the fenced state is terminal.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/guarantees.md#L207-L228",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9ffbfd6f0fecc7a0a8c6c009d28aa353e044dfaab8603136584569807a45b895:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0e90c1b614db4765b1231c823c80f633",
      "statement": "There are two durability proof sources: a bucket proof uploads the LTX data and reads the ownership record once, acknowledging only if it still names this node at this epoch; a fleet proof needs no read because a takeover seals a member before restoring so a stale owner's ack-all fails closed.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/output_gate.rs#L173-L212",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5fc9ab050354091b407d2391b1a217f89ea1cbfa33c9beb523726911f448e551:"
        },
        {
